  "prefLabel": "Puc 2105.07 Joint Advertising and Marketing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 2105.07 Joint Advertising and Marketing.\n\n(a) A utility shall not engage in joint advertising or marketing programs of any sort directly or indirectly with its competitive energy affiliates.\n\n(b) This section shall not prohibit a utility from participating, on a nondiscriminatory basis, in non-sales meetings with its competitive energy affiliates or any non-affiliated energy competitor to discuss technical or operational subjects.\n\nSource. #7884-A, eff 5-2-03, EXPIRED: 5-2-11\n\nNew. #9921, eff 5-3-11; ss by #10909, eff 8-8-15; ss by #14556, eff 4-15-26, EXPIRES: 4-15-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc2100.html"
